#!/usr/bin/python3
"""CPZ Search: one fzf popup for actions, apps, Settings, files, the calculator
and tmux buffers.

Started by Alt+O from /etc/tmux.conf. The popup opens like a search box with the
apps installed through the Applications manager, the mounted USB media, one row
per Settings page, the daily CPZ tmux actions and the power actions; typing
anything loads the rest (catalog apps and PATH commands). A leading prefix
switches the provider, in the same spirit as Walker in Omarchy:
    /      files under $HOME and the small system configuration roots
    =      calculator
    apps   Terminal Trove apps (installed first, the rest can be installed)
    $      tmux paste buffers

There is no daemon, index or new package. fzf, find, file, tmux and python3 are
already part of the image; the search runs only while the popup is open.

The item format is "kind<US>payload<US>display<US>extra<US>flags". Only the
display field is shown (--with-nth=3); fzf matches against that visible field,
which is why file paths are absolute (a leading "/" selects and matches them)
and the calculator line starts with the original expression. The hidden extra
field holds the command to run for a Terminal Trove app, and flags record
whether that app is installed, managed or installable.
"""

